{"explanation": "Repair only establish. Preserve the measured frame-0 bowl, counter and cabinet geometry and the acknowledged absence of motion. Exclude the unresolved cooktop-adjacent sector 3. Examine sector 7 first, then sector 0 only if needed, using their persistent world landmarks rather than screen-relative identities. Each attempt requests four current depth points and two calibrated local crops. Revalidate bowl/support identity and numerical references, then test the actual transformed open-finger envelope with the original uncertainty, support, coverage and obstacle margins. No motion or gripper command is issued. Completion concerns fresh establishment of an alternative observed pregrasp region and usable cabinet support, not grasp acquisition.", "source": "def main(api):
    s, attempts = api.state(), []
    handoff = {"stage": "establish", "checkpoint_keys": ["establish.geometry", "establish.revision"], "frames": "World meters; xyzw tool quaternion; top-left image pixels in the named camera.", "acknowledged_actions_added": 0, "remaining_candidates": [7, 0], "limitations": ["No movement, grasp, retention or contact-depth test.", "Visible surface coverage is not hidden-volume clearance.", "The 4 mm minimum uncertainty allowance is engineering padding, not calibrated confidence.", "A local hover is not a checked route from the current hand pose.", "Revalidate affected references after movement; preserve the currently open hand."]}
    questions = {}
    for axis in ["x", "y", "z", "rx", "ry", "rz"]:
        questions[axis] = {"type": "choice", "instructions": "Subject: world " + axis + " component. Read state.processed_features.axes." + axis + ".goal_relation and state.processed_features.program.motion_authorized. Without authorization hold; otherwise decrease maps to negative, within_tolerance to hold, increase to positive.", "criteria": {"negative": "Authorized negative world translation or world rotation-vector component.", "hold": "No authorization or within tolerance.", "positive": "Authorized positive world translation or world rotation-vector component."}}
    questions["gripper"] = {"type": "choice", "instructions": "Subject: gripper. Read state.processed_features.objective.gripper and state.processed_features.program.motion_authorized. This observation stage has no motion authorization: keep the gripper unchanged.", "criteria": {"open": "Explicitly authorized objective open for an observed empty hand.", "close": "Explicitly authorized objective close.", "keep": "No authorization, or objective keep; preserve actual hand state."}}
    def done(status, reason):
        evidence = {"initial_state": s, "attempts": attempts, "physical_actions": 0, "motion_authorized": False}
        api.checkpoint("establish.revision", evidence)
        return {"stage_status": status, "reason": reason, "evidence": evidence, "handoff": handoff, "completion_proposed": False}
    try:
        saved = api.recall("establish.geometry")
        refs = saved["value"]
        handoff["reference_provenance"] = {k: saved[k] for k in ["frame_id", "method_number", "source_sha256"] if k in saved}
        if s["frame_id"] != refs["frame_id"] or s["native_steps"] != refs["native_steps"]:
            return done("blocked", "Saved geometry is no longer from the current unmoved scene; reacquire bowl and support references before using this local repair.")
        if s["last_gripper_command"] != "open":
            return done("needs_replan", "Hand command changed since the empty-open observation; do not reopen or assume an empty hand.")
        bowl, support, own = refs["bowl"], refs["support"], s["own_geometry"]
        rim, center = np.asarray(bowl["rim_world_m"], dtype=float), np.asarray(bowl["circle"]["center_xy_m"], dtype=float)
        uncertainty = max(0.004, float(refs["uncertainty_floor_m"]))
        radius_bound = max(float(bowl["radius_bound_m"]), float(bowl["circle"]["radius_m"]) + float(bowl["circle"]["max_radial_error_m"]) + uncertainty)
        support_margin = float(support["inscribed_radius_m"]) - radius_bound
        if rim.shape != (8, 3) or not bool(np.isfinite(rim).all()) or support_margin < 0.012:
            return done("blocked", "Saved geometry fails the unchanged 12 mm support margin or rim validity check.")
        rotation = geo.rotation(s["tcp_quaternion_xyzw"])
        if float(rotation[2, 2]) > -0.98:
            return done("blocked", "The tool is no longer downward enough for this yaw-only envelope model.")
        lo, hi = own["finger_low_offset_tool_m"], own["finger_high_offset_tool_m"]
        corners = np.asarray([[x, y, z] for x in [lo[0], hi[0]] for y in [lo[1], hi[1]] for z in [lo[2], hi[2]]])
        fields = {"bowl_identity": ["same_upright_bowl", "changed", "unknown"], "support_identity": ["same_clear_patch", "changed", "unknown"], "hand_state": ["empty_open", "possibly_holding", "unknown"], "lip_identity": ["selected_bowl_lip", "unknown"], "inner_surface": ["visible_bowl_interior", "unknown"], "outer_surface": ["visible_counter", "obstructed", "unknown"], "local_visibility": ["visible_no_overhang", "occluded_or_overhang", "unknown"], "note": {"type": "string", "maxLength": 600}}
        for index in [7, 0]:
            if api.state()["budgets"]["gpt_remaining"] < 1:
                return done("yield", "No review budget remains for the next distinct candidate; use the saved partial measurements and remaining_candidates.")
            handoff["remaining_candidates"] = [i for i in handoff["remaining_candidates"] if i != index]
            rec = {"sector_index": index, "reference_frame_id": refs["frame_id"]}
            attempts.append(rec)
            try:
                g = rim[index].copy()
                radial = (g[:2] - center) / np.linalg.norm(g[:2] - center)
                tangent = np.asarray([radial[1], -radial[0]])
                yaw = math.atan2(float(radial[1]), float(radial[0])) - math.atan2(float(rotation[1, 1]), float(rotation[0, 1]))
                q = api.compose(s["tcp_quaternion_xyzw"], [0.0, 0.0, math.atan2(math.sin(yaw), math.cos(yaw))])
                offsets = (corners - np.asarray(own["pad_center_in_tool_m"])) @ geo.rotation(q).T
                uv_bounds = np.column_stack((offsets[:, :2] @ tangent, offsets[:, :2] @ radial))
                low, high = np.min(uv_bounds, axis=0) - uncertainty - 0.006, np.max(uv_bounds, axis=0) + uncertainty + 0.006
                volume = np.asarray([[float(v[0]), float(v[1]), z] for a in [low[0], high[0]] for b in [low[1], high[1]] for v in [g[:2] + a * tangent + b * radial] for z in [-refs["counter"]["plane"][3] - 0.005, float(g[2]) + 0.10]])
                crops = {}
                for name, camera in [("local_eye", "robot0_eye_in_hand"), ("local_agent", "agentview")]:
                    cal = api.camera(camera)
                    if cal["frame_id"] != s["frame_id"]:
                        raise RuntimeError("Camera frame changed; projected regions are stale.")
                    camera_points = geo.transform(volume, np.linalg.inv(np.asarray(cal["camera_to_world_opencv"])))
                    if float(np.min(camera_points[:, 2])) <= 0:
                        raise RuntimeError("Local observation volume projects behind a camera.")
                    hp = camera_points @ np.asarray(cal["K"]).T
                    pixels = hp[:, :2] / hp[:, 2:3]
                    lower, upper = np.floor(np.min(pixels, axis=0)) - 6, np.ceil(np.max(pixels, axis=0)) + 6
                    box = [max(0, int(lower[0])), max(0, int(lower[1])), min(767, int(upper[0])), min(767, int(upper[1]))]
                    if box[2] - box[0] < 8 or box[3] - box[1] < 8:
                        raise RuntimeError("Candidate is outside a usable complementary camera crop.")
                    crops[name] = {"camera": camera, "box": box, "stride": 4}
                context = {"candidate_sector_index": index, "candidate_lip_world_m": g.tolist(), "bowl_center_xy_m": center.tolist(), "radial_world_xy": radial.tolist(), "tangent_world_xy": tangent.tolist(), "padded_envelope_local_xy_m": [low.tolist(), high.tolist()], "local_coordinates": "First tangent, second radial, centered on the selected lip.", "support_polygon_xy_m": support["polygon_xy_m"], "support_plane": support["plane"], "support_anchor": refs["selected_depth_points"]["check1"], "regions_to_request": crops, "previous_failure": "Sector 3 had observed cooktop intrusion at the envelope edge. It is excluded; this is a different physical rim sector.", "uncertainty_floor_m": uncertainty}
                r = api.review("Inspect this NEW sector, not old sector 3. Request points lip on its actual uppermost lip material (radius=1), inner on visible bowl interior 35-50 mm radially inward, outer on visible counter 35-50 mm radially outward, both near the tangent center, and support on the supplied cabinet-top anchor. Use current pixels and successful visible depth, not hidden surfaces or substituted background. Request regions local_eye and local_agent using the exact camera, box and stride entries in regions_to_request. Inspect the whole padded envelope in both images for unobserved portions, overhangs and neighboring objects. visible_no_overhang describes observed coverage only, never hidden-space certification. A visible low plate or counter under the envelope is not automatically a collision; measured heights will be tested. Confirm the same upright patterned bowl, same fully visible clear cabinet support polygon and empty-open hand. Return all declared fields; distinguish unknown from changed.", context=context, fields=fields)
                bad = [e["name"] for e in r["measurement_errors"]]
                points = {n: r["points"][n] for n in ["lip", "inner", "outer", "support"] if n in r["points"] and n not in bad and r["points"][n]["frame_id"] == r["frame_id"]}
                rec.update({"frame_id": r["frame_id"], "parameters": r["parameters"], "points": points, "measurement_errors": r["measurement_errors"], "crops": crops, "candidate_lip_world_m": g.tolist()})
                api.checkpoint("establish.revision", {"initial_state": s, "attempts": attempts, "physical_actions": 0})
                p, now = r["parameters"], api.state()
                if r["status"] == "stop":
                    return done("abort", r["explanation"])
                if now["native_steps"] != s["native_steps"] or now["frame_id"] != s["frame_id"] or r["frame_id"] != s["frame_id"]:
                    return done("needs_replan", "Unexpected scene advancement during observation; references need reacquisition.")
                if p["bowl_identity"] == "changed" or p["support_identity"] == "changed" or p["hand_state"] == "possibly_holding":
                    return done("needs_replan", "Fresh review invalidates stationary upright bowl, clear support, or empty-hand assumptions.")
                required = {"bowl_identity": "same_upright_bowl", "support_identity": "same_clear_patch", "hand_state": "empty_open", "lip_identity": "selected_bowl_lip", "inner_surface": "visible_bowl_interior", "outer_surface": "visible_counter", "local_visibility": "visible_no_overhang"}
                if any(p[k] != v for k, v in required.items()) or len(points) != 4:
                    raise RuntimeError("Candidate identity, visibility or required depth unresolved: " + str(p) + "; successful points=" + str(list(points)) + "; errors=" + str(r["measurement_errors"]))
                lip, top = np.asarray(points["lip"]["world_m"]), np.asarray(points["support"]["world_m"])
                if float(np.linalg.norm(lip - g)) > 0.006 or abs(float(top @ np.asarray(support["plane"][:3]) + support["plane"][3])) > 0.004 or float(np.linalg.norm(top - np.asarray(refs["selected_depth_points"]["check1"]["world_m"]))) > 0.006:
                    raise RuntimeError("Fresh lip or support depth disagrees with the stationary reference beyond its fixed margin.")
                for name, sign in [("inner", -1), ("outer", 1)]:
                    point = np.asarray(points[name]["world_m"])
                    d = point[:2] - g[:2]
                    if not 0.025 <= sign * float(d @ radial) <= 0.055 or abs(float(d @ tangent)) > 0.025 or float(point[2]) > float(g[2]) - 0.012:
                        raise RuntimeError(name + " depth does not establish the selected lower finger neighborhood.")
                clouds = [np.asarray(r["regions"][n]["world_m"], dtype=float) for n in crops if n in r["regions"] and n not in bad and r["regions"][n]["frame_id"] == r["frame_id"] and "world_m" in r["regions"][n] and len(r["regions"][n]["world_m"]) > 0]
                if not clouds:
                    raise RuntimeError("No successful current local point cloud; summarized or missing depth is insufficient.")
                cloud = np.concatenate(clouds, axis=0)
                cloud = cloud[np.isfinite(cloud).all(axis=1)]
                uv = np.column_stack(((cloud[:, :2] - g[:2]) @ tangent, (cloud[:, :2] - g[:2]) @ radial))
                mask = ((uv >= low) & (uv <= high)).all(axis=1)
                if int(np.sum(mask)) < 30:
                    raise RuntimeError("Fewer than 30 visible samples cover the actual padded finger envelope.")
                gap = max(float(np.min(np.linalg.norm(uv[mask] - np.asarray([a, b]), axis=1))) for a in np.linspace(float(low[0]), float(high[0]), 5) for b in np.linspace(float(low[1]), float(high[1]), 15))
                external_high = (np.linalg.norm(cloud[:, :2] - center, axis=1) > radius_bound) & (cloud[:, 2] > float(g[2]) - 0.015)
                rec["metrics"] = {"coverage_gap_m": gap, "envelope_samples": int(np.sum(mask)), "external_high_samples": int(np.sum(mask & external_high)), "support_remaining_margin_m": support_margin, "uncertainty_floor_m": uncertainty}
                if gap > 0.008 or bool(np.any(mask & external_high)):
                    raise RuntimeError("Unchanged 8 mm sampling limit or neighboring high-surface exclusion failed: " + str(rec["metrics"]))
                surface_z = float(np.max(cloud[mask, 2]))
                hover = [float(g[0]), float(g[1]), surface_z + 0.025 - float(np.min(offsets[:, 2]))]
                approach = {"reference_key": "establish.geometry", "frame_id": r["frame_id"], "native_steps": now["native_steps"], "selected_sector_index": index, "supersedes_old_grasp_index": refs["grasp_index"], "lip_world_m": g.tolist(), "radial_world_xy": radial.tolist(), "tangent_world_xy": tangent.tolist(), "candidate_quaternion_xyzw": q, "open_finger_offsets_world_m": offsets.tolist(), "padded_local_envelope_m": [low.tolist(), high.tolist()], "observed_max_surface_z_m": surface_z, "local_hover_pad_world_m": hover, "hover_lowest_finger_margin_m": 0.025, "radius_bound_m": radius_bound, "uncertainty_floor_m": uncertainty, "fresh_depth_points": points, "metrics": rec["metrics"], "interpretation": p, "motion_authorized": False, "control_question_keys": list(questions), "limitations": handoff["limitations"]}
                api.checkpoint("establish.approach", approach)
                handoff.update({"checkpoint_keys": ["establish.geometry", "establish.revision", "establish.approach"], "authoritative_approach_key": "establish.approach", "selected_sector_index": index, "freshness": {"frame_id": r["frame_id"], "native_steps": now["native_steps"]}, "reference_reuse": "Original measured rim, support polygon and counter are unchanged-frame data, checked against fresh identity and lip/support depths. Keep original sector 3 failure as evidence; use the new approach key instead of its grasp_index.", "next_scope": "Establish the actual swept route and contact configuration before acquisition. No hidden under-lip shape, attachment transform, base offset or transport clearance is supplied."})
                return done("stage_complete", "Fresh RGB-D evidence establishes a different accessible local rim sector with unchanged uncertainty and clearance margins, and revalidates the sufficiently large cabinet support patch. No physical action or grasp is claimed.")
            except Exception as e:
                rec["gap"] = str(e)[:1800]
                api.checkpoint("establish.revision", {"initial_state": s, "attempts": attempts, "physical_actions": 0})
        return done("blocked", "Both distinct replacement sectors exhausted; unresolved measurements and fixed-margin failures are recorded. Latest gap: " + attempts[-1]["gap"])
    except Exception as e:
        return done("blocked", "Observation repair could not validate its required references: " + str(e)[:1800])
", "interface": "Executable Python main(api), using only provided np, math and geo globals. Returns stage_status, reason, evidence, handoff and completion_proposed=false. At most two reviews of distinct sectors, zero Jev calls and zero native steps, below the 24-call/72-step slice limits. stage_complete requires current semantic identity/visibility checks, successful fresh depth checks, at least 12 mm retained support margin, sufficient envelope sampling, at most 8 mm coverage gap and no measured neighboring high-surface intrusion. Missing evidence or fixed-margin failure returns blocked with diagnostics; changed assumptions return needs_replan; review stop returns abort; unavailable review budget returns yield. establish.geometry remains unchanged, preserving original calibrated geometry and the sector-3 failure. establish.revision saves current state, successful partial measurements, errors, crop specifications, candidate indices and numerical diagnostics. On success establish.approach saves the authoritative replacement sector, current frame/native-step provenance, world geometry, candidate xyzw orientation, own-finger offsets, padded envelope, local hover estimate and limitations. Handoff identifies which key supersedes the old grasp_index, necessary frames, reference dependencies, remaining candidates and unverified facts. Checkpoints contain no dense point clouds or future control code.", "jev_protocol": "The source defines exactly seven control questions: x, y, z, rx, ry, rz and gripper. Each axis explicitly binds to state.processed_features.axes.<axis>.goal_relation and the program motion_authorized gate. Negative and positive mean decreasing/increasing world translation coordinates or negative/positive world rotation-vector components; hold means unauthorized or within tolerance. The gripper question binds to objective.gripper: open and close require explicit authorization, while keep preserves the actual hand. motion_authorized is false throughout this observation-only method, so no api.control, api.drive or api.choose is called. Jev is not used as an image sensor, metric calculator or clearance oracle. Program numerical features come from successful RGB-D measurements, calibrated projections, preserved same-frame fits and current own geometry: reference discrepancies, a minimum 4 mm engineering allowance, a 12 mm support margin, transformed padded finger bounds, sampled coverage gaps, neighboring surface heights and a 25 mm local hover margin. Review interpretations are checked separately from these numerical tests. No pose receipt or gripper closure is treated as object-effect evidence; there are no new physical receipts. Bounded feedback consists of one fresh review per distinct candidate, saving partial evidence before testing or retrying. Failed membership, depth, identity, visibility or geometry checks never relax margins or declare occluded space free. After two candidates the method returns the exact remaining gaps, rather than asking the old sector-3 question again. A successful stage requires fresh observational effect evidence and still makes no whole-task completion claim."}
